  "id": "nervemuscle-preparation",
  "term": "nerve–muscle preparation",
  "definition": "In historical physiology, a nerve–muscle preparation is an experimental setup consisting of a nerve connected to a muscle, used to observe how stimulation of the nerve affects muscular contraction. In the passage, it is used to illustrate that a muscle may contract when a steady electrical stimulus is withdrawn, especially if the withdrawal is sudden.",
